0. About this license

This is a source-available license. It is not an open-source license. It
has not been approved by the Open Source Initiative, and it does not grant
the freedoms the Open Source Definition requires. It lets anyone read the
source of the Covered Software and lets individuals use it for their own
Personal Use. It reserves every other use, and all publication and
distribution, to the Licensor.


1. Definitions

1.1  "Licensor" means Nathan Slaughter.

1.2  "Covered Software" means the software and associated project
     materials that this license accompanies and that the Licensor has the
     right to license, in any version, and any portion of them. It includes
     source code, object code, documentation, examples, templates,
     configuration formats, schemas, tests, fixtures, and data files. It
     does not include Third-Party Components or Outputs.

1.3  "Modification" means any change to, addition to, deletion from,
     translation of, or other work based on any portion of the Covered
     Software. Every restriction this license places on the Covered
     Software also applies to Modifications.

1.4  "Third-Party Component" means software or other material that is
     included with or used by the Covered Software and is licensed by
     someone other than the Licensor under separate terms.

1.5  "You" means the natural person exercising rights under this license.

1.6  "Eligible Individual" means a natural person who uses the Covered
     Software only on their own behalf, not on behalf of an Organization.

1.7  "Personal Use" means private use by an Eligible Individual for their
     own purposes, such as learning, study, and personal projects. It does
     not include use in a trade or business, including the individual's
     own; work for an employer or other Organization; evaluating the
     Covered Software, or the Licensor's services, for an Organization;
     services to clients or other persons; or redistribution.

1.8  "Organization" means any company, partnership, trust, fund,
     association, government body, nonprofit, or other entity that is not a
     natural person.

1.9  "Public Project" means any project, repository, package, product,
     publication, or service that is available to the public or to any
     group of people beyond You, whether it is free, paid, commercial,
     nonprofit, source available, or open source.

1.10 "Published Code" means source code, object code, or other code that
     is published, distributed, or otherwise made available to any person
     other than You, in any form and by any means.

1.11 "Hosted Service" means making the Covered Software, or functionality
     it provides, available over a network to any person other than You,
     including as a web application, API, or managed service.

1.12 "Output" means data, files, and other results that the Covered
     Software generates from Your inputs or retrieves at Your request.

1.13 "Written Permission" means permission that meets section 9.

1.14 "Contributor" means any person other than the Licensor whose
     contribution the Licensor has accepted into the Covered Software.


2. Grants

2.1  Reading the source. Any natural person, including one acting for an
     Organization, may view, download, and clone the source of the Covered
     Software in order to read it, and may keep private copies for that
     purpose. This section grants no right to run, install, or modify the
     Covered Software, or to do anything section 4 reserves.

2.2  Personal use. If You are an Eligible Individual and You comply with
     this license, the Licensor grants You a personal, non-exclusive,
     non-transferable, non-sublicensable, royalty-free license, for
     Personal Use only, to:

     (a) download, install, and run the Covered Software;
     (b) make the copies reasonably necessary for that use, including
         private backups; and
     (c) make private Modifications and run them.

2.3  Your copies and Modifications must stay private: kept on devices,
     accounts, and storage that only You can access.

2.4  This license grants no right to publish, distribute, sublicense,
     sell, lend, or otherwise supply the Covered Software or any
     Modification to anyone else, except as Written Permission allows.
     Section 6 covers Outputs.

2.5  All rights not expressly granted are reserved. No right is granted by
     implication, estoppel, or otherwise. No trademark right is granted.


3. Organizations

Organizations, and individuals using the Covered Software on an
Organization's behalf, including for an employer or to evaluate the
Covered Software or the Licensor's services for an Organization, are
outside the grant in section 2.2. They must obtain Written Permission
before any use other than reading the source as section 2.1 allows.


4. Public projects, published code, and reserved uses

4.1  No person may incorporate the Covered Software, any portion of it, or
     any Modification into any Public Project or any Published Code without
     the Licensor's prior express Written Permission. This applies whether
     the receiving project is free, paid, commercial, nonprofit, source
     available, or open source.

4.2  The following uses are also reserved. Each requires the Licensor's
     prior express Written Permission, whether or not the Covered Software
     has been modified:

     (a) publishing, redistributing, sublicensing, selling, lending, or
         otherwise supplying copies to anyone else;
     (b) public forks and other public copies of the source, except as
         section 4.4 provides;
     (c) vendoring the source into other software;
     (d) packages, and binaries, executables, or archives that contain the
         code;
     (e) container images and virtual-machine images that contain the code;
     (f) notebooks or other documents that contain copied code; and
     (g) Hosted Services that incorporate the Covered Software.

4.3  Written Permission to use the Covered Software for an Organization
     does not include any right under this section unless it says so
     expressly.

4.4  Where the Licensor makes the source of the Covered Software available
     in a public repository on GitHub, GitHub's Terms of Service give
     GitHub users a license to view public repositories and to reproduce
     them on GitHub by forking, as GitHub's functionality permits. This
     license does not restrict those rights, and sections 2.3, 2.4, 4.1,
     and 4.2(a) and (b) do not apply to a fork made and kept on GitHub in
     that way. This exception goes no further than GitHub's terms:

     (a) beyond what GitHub's terms grant, and the reading section 2.1
         allows, it gives no right to use the Covered Software; section
         2.2 or Written Permission governs any other use;
     (b) it does not permit publishing Modifications, including by
         committing them to a public fork; and
     (c) it does not permit copying the Covered Software from GitHub, or
         from a fork, into any other Public Project or Published Code.


5. Local operation

5.1  Running the Covered Software on a machine You control, for Your own
     Personal Use, is not a Hosted Service.

5.2  Letting any other person use the Covered Software or its
     functionality through an interface You run is a Hosted Service under
     section 4.2(g) and requires Written Permission.


6. Outputs

6.1  Outputs are not Covered Software. The Licensor claims no ownership,
     through this license, of Your inputs, Your Outputs, or third-party
     data.

6.2  This license does not restrict sharing Outputs.

6.3  Material of the Covered Software that is taken out of an Output and
     used separately, such as templates, stylesheets, markup structure, or
     code, remains Covered Software. Section 6.2 does not permit publishing
     the Covered Software or any code.

6.4  You are responsible for complying with the terms of any data provider
     or service whose data an Output contains.


7. Third-party components

Third-Party Components are licensed under their own terms, and those terms
govern them. This license does not restrict any right those terms grant,
and the Licensor claims no rights in material he does not own. If this
license and a Third-Party Component's license conflict about that
component, the component's own license controls.


8. Notices

Keep the copyright notice, this license, and any notice files the Covered
Software includes, such as notices of Third-Party Components, intact in
every copy and Modification. Do not remove or alter the notices the
Covered Software displays.


9. Written Permission

9.1  Written Permission must be express, in writing, and sent or signed by
     the Licensor. It must identify the recipient, the permitted scope, any
     duration, and any publication or distribution rights.

9.2  None of the following is Written Permission: an inquiry, silence, a
     lack of objection, an automatic reply, attribution, a donation, or the
     purchase of an unrelated product.

9.3  Written Permission grants only what it states. On any matter it does
     not address, this license applies.

9.4  Send requests to git@nathanslaughter.com.


10. Acceptance

By downloading, installing, copying, modifying, or using the Covered
Software, You accept this license. If You do not accept it, You have no
right to do any of those things. If You are not an Eligible Individual and
have no Written Permission, You may not use the Covered Software, except to
read its source as section 2.1 allows.


11. Termination

11.1 Your rights under this license end automatically if You breach it.

11.2 The Licensor may reinstate terminated rights in writing.

11.3 When Your rights end, You must stop using the Covered Software and
     delete the copies and Modifications in Your possession. You may keep
     the Outputs You generated, subject to section 6.


12. Survival

Sections 1, 6.1, 6.3, 6.4, 7, 11.3, and 12 through 18 survive the end of
Your rights under this license.


